    "illustrator": "Rafia Bano",
    "publisher": "Eklavya",
    "pageCount": "16",
    "description": "A golden yellow sun, blazes across the sky, an invitation to grey clouds. Soon they burst open and rain descends accompanied by rain, thunder and lightning. A cool monsoon breeze\r\n  starts to blow bringing welcome relief. Encompassing as it does, two quintessentially Indian elements - with the monsoons in the narrative and the innovative use of zardoshi embroidery for the\r\n  illustrations makes this simple story book strike home."
